renderer_version: 2.0.0
payload_contract_version: sda.gtm-analysis/2.0.0
diagnosis_contract_version: sda.gtm-diagnosis/1.0.0
note: three-tab GTM diagnostic (Summary, Drivers, Outlook) on the shared finance shell and the reference report design system (dark-grey banner, lime accent, mono labels, dark table headers, square corners, light and dark themes), with a tab-aware glossary. template.html and gtm_analytics.css are carried over from the finance renderer 1.4.0. Built from governed extracts by scripts/build_gtm_dashboard.py (outputs/gtm_diagnostic_<as-of>.html) or from a local workbook by scripts/build_sample_dashboard.py (docs/gtm_dashboard_sample.html); both share scripts/gtm/render.py. Layout in wireframes/gtm_wireframe.html. Specification: references/dashboard-contract.md.
1.2.0: governed mode. The renderer reads pipeline.coverage.headline (governed: all open ÷ the quarter's pipeline target; local: by expected close quarter), pipeline.py (open and weighted a year earlier, with engine-emitted changes), pipeline.late_stage_label, conversion.win_rate_value and capabilities.loss_reasons (no loss reasons: a won-and-lost panel instead). Payload additions only; contract unchanged.
1.2.1: the Window and Compare toggles stay on the right of the title at desktop width, as on the finance page (they wrap below only under 980px); the scope line keeps scope, USD and months of history.
1.2.1: governed source defaults to PROD_DB.SEMANTIC_VIEWS.GTM_ANALYTICS (build_gtm_dashboard.py --source), shown in the banner.
1.2.2: live builds read loss reasons (optional gtm-conv-loss extract on OPPORTUNITY_LINE_ITEM.LOSS_REASON); the won-and-lost fallback now says no loss reasons were supplied rather than that the view has none. Copy only; contract unchanged.
1.3.0: Pipeline risk tab, first and opened by default: deals not closing (past due or close date pushed out), customers stuck in a stage (over 2x the median stay of other customers), high-value deals (top 10% by ACV) and lost deals per window, in recurring ACV (one-off product families excluded). Reads payload.risk and lenses[x].lost (payload additions; contract unchanged).
1.3.1: runs on either view schema (v1 deployed, v2 semantic_view.yml; meta.view_schema in the footer); "new / upsell split not available" when the view has no subscription type. Copy only; contract unchanged.
1.4.0: three tabs on the finance renderer 1.6.0 layout and CSS: Pipeline (opens first), Bookings, Outlook. Pipeline and Bookings each lead with an executive summary of 3 to 5 engine-built bullets and side cards, then a figure strip at a glance, then one chart beside the decisions for management; every table and deal list moved into drill-downs. Pipeline bullets and cards centre on days to win (new: lenses[].velocity, pipeline.velocity_trend, optional gtm-velocity extract) and the share of open pipeline in high-value deals that are not closing or stuck (risk.at_risk). Bookings decisions are bookings-only (product decline, recurring-share drop, concentration). Outlook keeps coverage, closing this quarter, the scenario range and pipeline created, and states what the data cannot answer yet (renewals coming due, discounting). Finance-page wording: Data verified / From the data / Test data, not yet AI reviewed, suggested owners · for discussion, at stake. Driver ids keep '+' (Tracking+ no longer collides with Tracking). Payload additions only; contract unchanged.
1.5.0: every executive-summary bullet is one short line on the page (the bold lead plus a line of at most 15 words without figures, engine-built as `short`); clicking it opens the full sentence above the evidence it drills to. Decisions for management show the first question clause (at most 12 words, `short`) and open the full question the same way. One fixed light theme: the dark-mode variant is removed and the page declares color-scheme light only. Payload additions only; contract unchanged.
1.5.0: October-2026 review fixes. One analysis date (the bookings month-end): headline pipeline from the PIPELINE_OVERVIEW snapshot (gtm-cards-snapshot), deal lists labelled current state with a snapshot-to-current reconciliation; as_of_alignment QC. Coverage = in-quarter open ÷ the quarter's pipeline-generation target (gtm-snapshot-ecq, gtm-targets-month), no 3.0x floor; created vs target to date (floor 100%). Bookings: order labels by largest measure with splits, re-papered pairs out of top orders, gross to net at line grain (gtm-gross-net), organic view, breadth before 'broad-based', rest-of-year scenario, AOV rule. Stage age vs P90 of non-zero runs (gtm-stage-p90); value win rate excluding negative-ACV wins, count rate on deals of $5k or more (gtm-conv-size). Thresholds in meta and the glossary. Layout: the side cards are a row between the executive summary and the strip.
1.6.0: Pipeline tab leads with High value contracts at a glance (open deals of $100k ACV or more, one definition for every high-value figure): days to win, deals at risk, not closing and stuck read only high-value deals; the deal lists leave the drawers for a table with a list selector, five rows and an Others row that opens the rest. Weighted pipeline is off the page (strip, tiles, coverage chart, drawers); the scenario is in-quarter open pipeline x the last-twelve-month win rate by value and by count. Bookings: Top five customers and Largest order are their own cards; gross-to-net and rest-of-year sit under Bookings at a glance. Outlook: bookings by subscription status is its own section (table left, facts right) under the tiles; won vs booked leads the charts; the monthly pipeline-created chart moves into the Pipeline created drill-down.
1.6.1: the page is written to outputs/yes_energy_pipeline_risk_readout.html (no month in the name, so a scheduled daily run rewrites the same file); when a run is for a later month than the page already there, that page is kept as outputs/previous/yes_energy_pipeline_risk_readout.html and since_last compares with it.
1.6.0: one coverage definition. Coverage = weighted (probability-weighted) pipeline at the headline date ÷ the pipeline targets (PIPELINE_TARGET by TARGET_MONTH) of the three calendar months after that date's month, read against the --coverage-floor (1.0x governed); blank (—) with a QC warning and a load-targets ask when any of the three months has no target. Replaces the governed PIPELINE_COVERAGE_RATIO_QTD headline and the in-quarter generation ratio (the view metric stays in the glossary). gtm-targets-month is now a required extract. Reads pipeline.coverage.headline {basis: next_3_months, numerator: weighted, anchor, months, label, targets_by_month, open, weighted, value, target, floor, shortfall, missing_months, quarter, in_quarter, quarter_target}; tiles, drawers and glossary name the window. Payload additions only; contract unchanged.
1.7.0: Compare = vs Prior quarter, replacing vs Prior year. Every lens is <WINDOW>_pq: the same months one quarter earlier, so both sides have the same length (Month and Quarter to date: Oct 2026 vs Jul 2026; Last twelve months: Nov 25–Oct 26 vs Aug 25–Jul 26). Year to date has no prior-quarter equivalent: YTD_pq is available: false with a reason and its Window button is disabled with that reason as the tooltip; the page opens on Quarter to date. Inside lenses the comparison keys are renamed py → cmp (range.cmp_label, cmp_short, conversion_cmp, conv_size_cmp, velocity.cmp, lost.cmp, orders_cmp, count_cmp, closed_cmp, top_customers[].cmp); outside lenses py still means a real prior year and is unchanged: monthly trend lines and the range-bar mark, open and weighted pipeline a year earlier (pipeline.py, the view's PY twins: there are no prior-quarter twins), the rest-of-year scenario and the seasonal tests. Bridges run Prior quarter → This period. The BOOKINGS_OVERVIEW tie-out checks every window's current total (YTD included) and no longer the PY twins; gross to net ties to the quarter-to-date total. compare.py reads LTM_pq. Contract bumped to sda.gtm-analysis/2.0.0 (lens ids, basis and key renames).
1.8.0: merge repair. The prior-quarter basis (1.7.0) and the 1.6.x layout are combined: High value contracts at a glance (cards on the prior-quarter basis, filling the row when fewer than four; deal tables), Coverage = weighted pipeline ÷ the next three months' targets as defined in 1.6.0 (N3), the weighted pipeline cell and bars off the page, Top five customers and Largest order cards, gross to net under Bookings at a glance, the subscription-status section, the keyed top-three waterfalls, the scenario against last year's won ACV. Fixes the blank page ('nc is not defined') left by the merge.
1.9.0: (originally built for the source org; renamed Yes Energy). No pipeline target, coverage, floor or weighted pipeline anywhere (the view holds no target; pipeline values are unweighted): the coverage cells, tiles, chart lines and glossary rows are removed; pipeline.by_close_quarter and pipeline.in_quarter replace pipeline.coverage. Quarters are fiscal (1 February to 31 January, FY named by the year it ends; meta.fiscal, shown as a chip). Measures read New sales and Seat expansion (recurring, Salesforce) and Non-recurring (NetSuite revenue); orders read as deals. No view-schema switch. Payload changes: pipeline.coverage, pipeline.weighted, meta.coverage_floor and meta.view_schema removed.
1.9.1: Outlook: 'What <months> must deliver' (the rest-of-fiscal-year scenario, as on Bookings) replaces the Renewals and discounting section, which is removed. Close quarters, 'Closing in' and the scenario are anchored on the date the deal values are from (the analysis month-end with gtm-snapshot-ecq, else the deal refresh date), so a quarter that has already ended no longer shows $0; the tile and chart state that date (pipeline.in_quarter.as_of, pipeline.close_quarters_as_of).
1.9.2: the 'What <months> must deliver' panel is on the Outlook tab only (removed from Bookings). Stage-run extracts may be split into gtm-stage-current-<n> chunks; dashboards.md sizes every extract to come back in the conversation.
1.9.3: validation fixes. Close quarters and the stage x quarter table come from the PIPELINE_OVERVIEW snapshot at the analysis date (gtm-snapshot-ecq by stage and close date) with past-due and later buckets, so both foot to the headline (QC close_quarters_foot); the deal-level risk stays current state and is labelled with its date, and its shares use that total. Outlook shows what has been won since the analysis date against the quarter scenario (and that the quarter has ended) and in the rest-of-year panel. Pipeline age uses the opportunity created date; the pipeline not yet counted as created (before 03 - EVALUATE) is stated. Stuck wording follows the rule in use (P90).
1.10.0: Outlook: 'What is in the pipeline?' leads with 3-5 drillable bullets (this quarter and next quarter: the range against what was won in the same quarter last year and what is already won; what the rest of the fiscal year must deliver against the same months last year; pipeline created; the risks in the open pipeline: not closing or stuck, over a year old, past due), each opening its drawer and every named figure opening its own; the KPIs stand in a highlighted column beside it (closing in the quarter, what it could deliver, open pipeline, pipeline created); the two chart rows are equal width and equal height (won vs booked | what the pipeline could deliver; open pipeline by close quarter | how old it is). A 'Favourable and unfavourable' sign and colour legend sits open above How to read this page on every tab, as on the finance page. The commentary selects and phrases engine fields only.
1.10.1: the variance legend (was 'Favourable and unfavourable') is headed 'Variance legend: how favourable and unfavourable moves are shown', in smaller type, with four columns: Outcome, Bar, Text colour and sign (the text itself in that colour, with an example figure: green with a plus sign, red in brackets, grey either sign, black in brackets) and Meaning; the separate Figure column is gone.
1.11.0: the AI review, as on the finance page. A diagnosis written by Claude for a view (contract sda.gtm-diagnosis/1.0.0, references/diagnosis.md) is admitted by scripts/gtm/diagnosis.py (every $ and % figure registered and resolving to the payload, no causal or forbidden wording, drill targets the page can open, every executive-tier driver and flagged risk block covered) and embedded as payload.diagnoses. The page then shows the written executive summary and decisions on the Pipeline and Bookings tabs, 'What this means' under Where the pipeline is at risk, What moved bookings and in the Outlook commentary, and the reviewed findings first in the driver drawer; the data badge and footer say 'AI reviewed' (was always 'not yet AI reviewed'), or 'This view not AI reviewed' on a view without one, which shows the engine reading. New: scripts/gtm_brief.py, validate_gtm_diagnosis.py, render_gtm_dashboard.py; build_gtm_dashboard.py takes --diagnosis and --allow-missing-review and publishes no page without the opening view's review.
2.0.0: Yes Energy, PROD_DB.SEMANTIC_VIEWS.GTM_ANALYTICS (exported 2026-11-23). Pipeline is WEIGHTED everywhere (ACV × Salesforce probability ÷ 100: WEIGHTED_OPEN_PIPELINE_ACV on lines, WEIGHTED_PIPELINE_VALUE_* on the cards, WEIGHTED_PIPELINE_ACV_ASAT on the snapshot; the loader maps them onto pipeline.open so close quarters, the stage grid and risk tiers are weighted and tie to the weighted card); unweighted is kept as context; pipeline created, won and lost stay unweighted. Fiscal year is the calendar year (January to December, FY named by that year; quarters Jan–Mar … Oct–Dec; common.FY_START_MONTH = 1). Recurring measures are ARR (New) (New Customer) and ARR (Upsell) (Upgrade, Renewal, Downgrade) from BOOKING_METRIC, replacing New sales / Seat expansion; Yes Energy stages Stage 0 … Invest (late stage = Align onwards); open filter NOT IS_CLOSED; DIM_PRODUCT added. Earlier entries describe the source-org build: their fiscal, stage and measure wording no longer applies.
